- **Photos** (was item 13, plus the video ask; 2026-09-10). Real photography on the home strip:
  23 photos + 1 video from a Cloudflare R2 bucket (`sagdi-photos`, public URL
  `https://pub-d80e4e9eb39747c9b6eeca7668d027ed.r2.dev`). How it works:
  - **Sets are folders.** `photos-src/<set>/` on Sagdi's machine (gitignored). `home/` is the home
    strip. A new block anywhere on the site is a new folder plus `listPhotos("<set>")`.
  - **Order is by filename.** Camera names sort by date; a number prefix (`010-…`) sorts ahead when
    manual control is wanted. Direction and captions in optional `set.json`:
    `{ "order": "newest-first" | "oldest-first", "items": { "<file>": { "alt", "caption" } } }`.
    Home is `newest-first`. All alt text is empty right now (digit-only filenames); fill via `items`.
  - **Sync:** `npm run photos:sync -- [<set>…] [--prune]`. Uploads a 720px-tall WebP (what the strip
    shows) and the 3000px JPEG original per photo, videos as-is, all named with a content hash and
    cached immutable. Already-present files are skipped, so a reorder or caption edit re-syncs in
    seconds. `--prune` deletes bucket files no longer in the folder; without it nothing is deleted.
    Manifest per set at `photos/<set>/manifest.json`; the site revalidates it hourly.
  - **Carousel loads the WebP straight from R2** (`unoptimized`), lazy with blur placeholder. Next's
    image optimizer is out of the path on purpose: it aborts upstream fetches at 7s
    (`node_modules/next/dist/server/image-optimizer.js` line 757) and on a home connection eight
    parallel 2 MB originals blew past that, showing as broken frames.
  - **Video frames** (`type: "video"` in the manifest) render as a muted, looping `<video>`, playing
    only while at least 60% of the frame is inside the strip and the strip is on screen, paused
    otherwise. Sizes come from the mp4's `tkhd` box (phone rotation handled) or `set.json`.
  - Verified in headless Chrome against the dev server: all 23 images render, video plays at the end
    of the strip, pauses when scrolled away, no-change sync uploads nothing.
  - Env: `PHOTOS_BASE_URL` (site, also in Vercel) + `R2_ACCOUNT_ID` (32-hex only), `R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID`,
    `R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `R2_BUCKET` (sync script only, local). `next.config.ts` still parses
    `PHOTOS_BASE_URL` at build time: a value without `https://` kills the build.
  - Not done, by choice: r2.dev is rate-limited and not edge-cached; a custom domain
    (`photos.sagdi.com`) needs sagdi.com's DNS on Cloudflare. Fine for now.
